DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] The MaineCare Third Party Liability (TPL) Exe
 mption Request and Attestation Form is Now Available
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			The MaineCare Third Party Liability (TPL) Exemption Req
 uest and Attestation Form is Now Available\nThe MaineCare Third Party Liab
 ility (TPL) Exemption Request and Attestation Form is Now Available\nOct 1
 3\, 2026\nOn\nAugust 3\, 2026\n\, MaineCare announced claims system update
 s to support proper TPL reimbursement processes in accordance with MaineCa
 re Benefits Manual (MBM)\, Chapter I\, Section 1.07 TPL rules. The\nMaineC
 are TPL Exemption Request and Attestation Form\nis now available for TPL e
 xemption request submission.\nRequesting TPL Exemption\nIn accordance with
  MBM\, Chapter I\, Section 1.07 rules\, MaineCare may assess the validity 
 of extenuating circumstance or service code TPL exemption requests to bill
  MaineCare as the primary payer for services delivered to a member with pr
 imary\, public\, or commercial coverage. Providers wishing to apply for TP
 L exemption to bill MaineCare as the primary payer must complete and submi
 t the\nMaineCare TPL Exemption Request and Attestation Form\nto the\nTPL M
 edicare Code Exempt Request email box\n.\nMaineCare will review completed 
 forms with the supporting documentation and provide a decision letter of a
 pproval or non-approval via email to the requestor. An exemption request a
 pproval letter is valid only for a specific member for a defined duration\
 , no greater than 12 months. The exemption request approval letter must be
  attached to all applicable MaineCare claims for dates of service during t
 he approved time. Claims without a valid and up-to-date approval letter ma
 y result in denials.\nProviders are responsible for maintaining exemption 
 request renewals by submitting a subsequent MaineCare\nTPL Exemption Reque
 st and Attestation Form\nat least 30 calendar days prior to the expiration
  date specified in the approval letter.\nLimited Retroactive TPL Exemption
  Review Period\nFor a limited time\, MaineCare will consider conti\nhttps:
 //www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/mainecare-third-part
 y-liability-tpl-exemption-request-and-attestation-form-now-available
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/mainecare-
 third-party-liability-tpl-exemption-request-and-attestation-form-now-avail
 able
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0682e47d62e4f8d5@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261013T224142Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Massage Therapy Awareness Week - October 25 t
 hrough 31
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, years of research have demonstrated the effectiven
 ess of massage therapy in a wide range of health treatments\, including pa
 in relief\, management of cancer symptoms\, reduction of depression\, and 
 overall enhancement of physical and mental well-being\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, m
 any individuals recognize the benefits of massage therapy for their health
  and turn to massage as a vital component of their health care regimen\; a
 nd\nWHEREAS\n\, Massage Therapy Awareness Week provides an opportunity for
  massage therapists across Maine to promote the health benefits of their p
 ractice and raise awareness in their communities about the essential role 
 massage therapy plays in maintaining and improving health\; and\nWHEREAS\n
 \, there are over 3\,000 licensed massage therapists serving the people of
  Maine and a dozen pre-approved massage therapy schools in Maine\; and\nWH
 EREAS\n\, Massage Therapy Awareness Week serves as a reminder of the impor
 tance of holistic approaches to health\, and the significant contributions
  of massage therapists in helping people live healthier\, more balanced li
 ves\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Govern
 or of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim the week of October 25-31\, 
 2026\, as\nMassage Therapy Awareness Week\nthroughout the State of Maine\,
  and I urge all citizens to recognize this observance.\nIn testimony where
 of\, I have caused\nthe Great Seal of the State to be\nhereunto affixed GI
 VEN under my\nhand at Augusta this eighth day of\nOctober Two Thousand Twe
 nty-Six\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamati
 ons/2026-10-massage-therapy-awareness-week-october-25-through-31
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-10-massage-therapy-awareness-week-october-25-through-31
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:8eaee101f5227860@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261013T224142Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Blindness Awareness Month - October
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\,\nblindness and low vision affect millions of America
 ns\, including an estimated 35\,000 Maine people\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nthe whi
 te cane and guide dog serve as essential tools that promote independence\,
  mobility\, and safety for people who are blind or have low vision\, and M
 aine law recognizes their use and provides protections for people who use 
 them\; and\nWHEREAS\,\npeople who are blind and or low vision contribute s
 ignificantly to the social\, cultural\, and economic vitality of our state
  as they pursue meaningful careers in diverse professions\, strengthen Mai
 ne's workforce\, raise families\, and enrich our communities through their
  participation in all aspects of life\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nwe honor the resil
 ience\, wisdom\, and lifelong contributions of older adults who are blind 
 or have low vision\, and their efforts to maintain independence while navi
 gating the unique challenges of aging with vision loss\; and\nWHEREAS\,\np
 eople with vision loss continue to encounter stigma\, discrimination\, and
  accessibility barriers\, including misconceptions about their capabilitie
 s and needs\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nwe recognize the efforts of vision rehabilit
 ation professionals\, educators\, self-advocates\, and allies across Maine
  who work to advance equality\, accessibility and opportunities for people
  who are blind or have low vision\; and\nWHEREAS\,\nBlindness Awareness Mo
 nth calls attention to the importance of accessibility\, inclusion\, and r
 espect\, and reminds us of the progress achieved through advocacy\, educat
 ion\, and civil rights protections\, as well as the work still to be done\
 ;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\,\nbe it resolved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of
  the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim October 2026 as\nBlindness Awaren
 ess Month\nin Maine\, and I call upon all residents to join in recognizing
  the contributions of Maine people who are blind or have low vision and to
  work together to promote accessibility\, inclusion\, independence\, and f
 ull participation in all aspects of community life.\nIn testimony whereof\
 , I have\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamat
 ions/2026-10-blindness-awareness-month-october
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-10-blindness-awareness-month-october
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:15df90ca2456269e@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261013T140732Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] System Remittance Advice (RA) and 835 Limitat
 ions
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			System Remittance Advice (RA) and 835 Limitations\nSyst
 em Remittance Advice (RA) and 835 Limitations\nOct 13\, 2026\nAttention Nu
 rsing Homes\, Hospitals\, and Private Non-Medical Institutions\, Appendix 
 C & F (PNMI-C-F): Claims RA/835 Issues\nFollowing the\nMIHMS upgrade\n\, t
 here are open issues affecting some RA/835s.  The issues are high priori
 ty for a fix that is underway\; we are currently targeting to fix the issu
 es by the end of October and will send another communication when the issu
 es have been resolved. This message provides details of the issues and ava
 ilable workarounds until the issues are fixed.\nCost of Care Reporting for
  Nursing Home\, Hospital Claims\, and PNMI-C-F\nNursing Home and Hospital 
 claims for members with cost of care are not being reported with the appro
 priate Claim Adjustment Reason Code (CARC) needed for balance billing memb
 ers.\nPDF RA – CARC 142 is not being reported for cost of care.\n835 –
  CARC 96 is being reported in error.\nAs a workaround until the fix is in 
 place\, MaineCare will provide a report that can be accessed on the\nMaine
 Care Partner Portal\n. On the Dashboard\, navigate to Reports > Other Repo
 rts > “Cost of Care Report.” This report will be available on Mondays 
 for the claims finalized on the prior Wednesday. Because this week’s cla
 ims will be finalized on Thursday\, the first report will be available no 
 later than Tuesday\, October 20\, 2026.\nSpenddown Reporting for Provider 
 Claims\nClaims with spenddown are not being reported with the appropriate 
 CARC needed for balance billing members.\nPDF RA – CARC 142 is not being
  reported for spenddown claims.\n835 – CARC 96 and/or CARC 178 is being 
 reported in error.\nAs a workaround until the fix is in place\, MaineCare 
 will provide a report that can be accessed on the MaineCare Partner Portal
 . On the dashboard\, navigate to Reports > Other Reports > “Spend Down R
 eport.” This\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletin
 s/system-remittance-advice-ra-and-835-limitations-2026-10-13
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/system-rem
 ittance-advice-ra-and-835-limitations-2026-10-13
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7adede86b9446278@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261012T151652Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261012
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Attention Trading Partners: the MaineCare Par
 tner Portal is Live
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Attention Trading Partners: the MaineCare Partner Porta
 l is Live\nAttention Trading Partners: the MaineCare Partner Portal is Liv
 e\nOct 12\, 2026\nAs an update to\nprevious communications\n\, we have lau
 nched the new\nMaineCare Partner Portal\n\, which replaces the previous He
 althPAS Online Portal. The MaineCare Partner Portal is now available for a
 ll regular functions\, 24 hours a day\, 7 days a week.\nAs a\nreminder\n\,
  starting today\, we are also changing how callers interact with and exper
 ience Provider Services and Member Services call center phone menus\, know
 n as Interactive Voice Response (IVR). A virtual assistant\, called Gabby\
 , will replace traditional phone menus by listening to what callers say to
  resolve simple inquiries.\nThis message includes information you will nee
 d to get started in the MaineCare Partner Portal. The link to the MaineCar
 e Partner Portal has not changed:\nmainecare.maine.gov\n.\nFor all informa
 tion about the upcoming changes to MIHMS\, see the MaineCare Partner Porta
 l section of the\nProvider Resources\npage. Please note that we have updat
 ed the\nFAQ\npreviously shared\, as of September 21\, 2026. For informat
 ion about the claims submission deadlines for the October 15\, 2026 and Oc
 tober 21\, 2026\, payment cycles\, please refer to the FAQ.\nMigrated Trad
 ing Partner Account Admin (R7) users\nComplete a one-time self-service pas
 sword reset. Click “Sign In” within the\nMaineCare Partner Portal\n\, 
 then click “Forgot Password” to reset your password. The “Forgot you
 r password?” feature is now a self-service tool! Provider Services will 
 not be able to assist with password resets.\nSet up a\nMulti-Factor Authen
 tication (MFA) method\n.\nSign into MaineCare’s Partner Portal.\nInvite 
 additional (delegated) users and assign permissions as appropriate. Refer 
 to the MaineCare Partner Portal Overview User Guide in the\nMMIS Learning 
 Center\n.\nFind step-by-s\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provid
 er-bulletins/attention-trading-partners-mainecare-partner-portal-live-2026
 -10-12
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/attention-
 trading-partners-mainecare-partner-portal-live-2026-10-12
