DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] MaineCare Telehealth Services Provider Licens
 ure Requirements
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			MaineCare Telehealth Services Provider Licensure Requir
 ements\nMaineCare Telehealth Services Provider Licensure Requirements\nOct
  05\, 2026\nAs a reminder\, all providers delivering telehealth services t
 o MaineCare members must be enrolled with MaineCare and must comply with M
 aineCare Benefits Manual\n(MBM) Chapter I\, Section 4: Telehealth Services
 \n.\nChapter I\, Section 4 requires that providers be\n“appropriately li
 censed\, accredited\, certified\, and/or registered in the state where the
  member is located during the provision of the telehealth service.”\nThi
 s means that all providers delivering in-person or telehealth services to 
 MaineCare members\, who are in Maine at the time of the service\, must hol
 d appropriate Maine credentials or Interstate Licensure Compacts recognize
 d by the\nDepartment of Professional and Financial Regulation\n(DPFR) or o
 ther appropriate organization.\nPursuant to\nMBM\, Ch. I\, Section 1.18\nf
 ailure to comply with these requirements can result in the denial of claim
 s or recoupment of payment because services delivered without proper state
  licensure are not eligible for reimbursement.\nFor questions\, please con
 tact your\nProvider Relations Specialist\n.\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/om
 s/providers/provider-bulletins/mainecare-telehealth-services-provider-lice
 nsure-requirements-2026-10-05
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/mainecare-
 telehealth-services-provider-licensure-requirements-2026-10-05
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
